---
description: Architecture and delivery guardrails for every change
alwaysApply: true
---

Read docs/guardrails.md before editing this repository.

Stay inside the approved products. Work in Next.js, FastAPI, Playwright, and the existing Terraform modules is normal work.

Stop before you edit anything when the task would add a product, datastore, language, or AWS service; replace a named product; skip an environment, Snyk, Playwright, Grafana k6, or OWASP ZAP; run the lite Playwright suite for a major release; mark a required step not applicable; edit a waiver; or change production IAM or Cognito.

Ask in one message, then wait:

- What you are trying to do
- Which rule blocks it
- Why the current architecture cannot do the job
- The smallest change that would break the rule
- Which pipeline steps would still run

Do not implement the deviation in the same turn. The user records approval under `deviations` in the change pack.
